commit 9264f40bc21c1dd461feb1ce1206e5ff38e8b9f5
Author: Abhi <57774784+Ichigo3766@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Apr 10 12:06:51 2026 -0700

    feat: speaker embedding support for Qwen3-TTS CustomVoice models (#148)
    
    * fix: handle mixed types in spkId and spkIsDialect for CustomVoice model
    
    The Qwen3-TTS CustomVoice config.json has:
      - spk_id: {"ryan": 3061, ...}  (single Int per speaker, not [Int])
      - spk_is_dialect: {"ryan": false, "eric": "sichuan_dialect", ...}  (Bool or String)
    
    The Base model had empty dicts {}, so these bugs were never hit.
    Added SpkIdValue and SpkDialectValue flexible decoders to handle both
    variants without breaking the Base model path.
    
    * feat: inject speaker embedding for CustomVoice models in prepareGenerationInputs
    
    For CustomVoice Qwen3-TTS models (ttsModelType == "custom_voice"):
    - Route voice name as `speaker` instead of `instruct` in generateVoiceDesign
    - Look up speaker name in talkerConfig.spkId map to get the integer speaker ID
    - Call talker.getInputEmbeddings() on that ID to produce a speaker embedding
    - Inject the speaker embedding between the codec prefix tokens and the
      pad+bos suffix in prepareGenerationInputs
    - Also apply dialect language ID override when spkIsDialect indicates a
      dialect speaker (e.g. Cantonese, Hokkien)
    
    This fixes voice identity not being preserved across sentences when using
    models like mlx-community/Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice-8bit.

